    Accepts a nested dictionary and returns a new dictionary by adding a key-value pair 
    to each inner dictionary. The key is the name of the inner dictionary (its key in the parent),
    and the value is the sum of all integer values in that inner dictionary.

    Only processes dictionaries that are direct values of the input dictionary.
    Recursively sums integers found at any depth within those inner dictionaries.
